sasha: FYI I opened PR #4555 to refresh the quickstart: canonical env var, Rust example (requested by infra), tiny Dockerfile for first deploy, and a short CLI auth flow example for attendees. Pls glance for compatibility with workshop slides.

mohit: nice. whats the canonical env var now? we had API_KEY, REDWOOD_TOKEN, etc.

sasha: REDWOOD_API_KEY only. added a migration note for LEGACY_TOKEN and a tiny snippet showing how to map old envs in CI.

rae: can you paste the Rust snippet? want to check crate name + sync vs async client shape.

sasha: sure, from the PR: 

```rust
use redwood_inference::Client;
use std::env;

fn main() -> Result<(), Box<dyn std::error::Error>> {
  let api_key = env::var("REDWOOD_API_KEY")?;
  let mut client = Client::new(&api_key)?;
  let resp = client.generate_sync("redwood-1", "hello quickstart")?;
  println!("{}", resp.output.text);
  client.close()?;
  Ok(())
}
```

mohit: couple of quick things: 1) crate is `redwood-inference` in Cargo.toml, 2) prefer `resp.output.text` (not resp.text), 3) add error handling in the sample comment. Also note minimum Rust edition 2021.

sasha: updated the PR with the crate name and a one-line comment about handling Result.

rae: on CLI auth  can you show a tiny call using `rwctl` (our CLI) to fetch ephemeral tokens for workshop folks? we've had lots of questions around ephemeral vs long-lived keys.

sasha: added a short CLI example: `rwctl auth exchange --key $REDWOOD_API_KEY --ttl 1h` and a curl fallback. left KMS details as a link to private deploy docs.

build-bot: docs PR #4555 staged build started.

mohit: Dockerfile check: keep it minimal for a first deploy. e.g., `FROM debian:bookworm-slim` for Rust users, install ca-certificates, copy binary, set CMD. maybe also provide a single-line build+run used in workshops: `docker build -t hello-rust . && docker run -e REDWOOD_API_KEY=$REDWOOD_API_KEY hello-rust`.

sasha: added a tiny Dockerfile + the one-liner to the README. also called out minimum Rust toolchain (1.70) and a note about static linking caveat for musl.

rae: can we avoid streaming in the main quickstart? lots of folks get stuck on handling partial failures. add streaming as an optional appendix.

sasha: yep, streaming moved to an "advanced" appendix. kept the main flow explicitly synchronous.

mohit: two broken links I found: the private deploy page (404) and the CLI docs anchor. I pasted corrected URLs in the PR comments.

sasha: thanks, fixed links. also added a troubleshooting section: 401 -> check REDWOOD_API_KEY + org allowlist, 429 -> check quota/usage dashboard, DNS errors -> proxy settings note.

docs-bot: PR #4555 labeled docs/quickstart and assigned to sasha. claimed by mohit for links and build sanity and by rae for copy clarity.

sasha: thanks all. ETA: will merge after mohit verifies the Docker build in CI and rae signs off on copy. planning to land this before next week's onboarding to avoid slide drift. :sparkles:
